{
  "schema": "touchline.coordinates/1",
  "description": "Where each programme plays, as a point. A sibling to programmes.json, in exactly the sense that file describes itself: a stable fact no collected page publishes, hand-resolved once and versioned, never geocoded at build time and never inferred from a slug. The point is the TOWN centroid the programme plays in — the fact programmes.json already holds — not the campus. A slug absent from this file renders the designed absence state: it is named and left unplotted, never dropped and never guessed.",
  "source": {
    "name": "U.S. Census Bureau, 2023 Gazetteer Files (Places, national)",
    "url": "https://www2.census.gov/geo/docs/maps-data/data/gazetteer/2023_Gazetteer/2023_Gaz_place_national.zip",
    "license": "Public domain (work of the U.S. federal government)",
    "method": "programmes.json `city` parsed as \"Town, AP-state\", the AP abbreviation mapped to its USPS code, then matched against the Gazetteer NAME with its legal descriptor (city/town/village/CDP) stripped. Incorporated places are preferred over CDPs where both exist. INTPTLAT/INTPTLONG are the internal point. Every row records the GEOID it resolved to, so any row can be re-checked against the source.",
    "resolved": "28 of 29 matched automatically; the 15 GLVC rows (2026-09-02) were matched the same way against the same file, Indianapolis to the consolidated-city 'city (balance)' row; the 22 RMAC and SSC rows (2026-09-02) likewise, Saint Leo to the Gazetteer's 'St. Leo town' and MSU Denver and Regis sharing Denver's point. The one that did not — Nashville — carries a `note` on its own row saying why, rather than being quietly corrected."
  },
